## Memory

- Keep this file concise and use it primarily as an index.
- Classify new durable knowledge by topic before writing it. Update the matching topic file, or create one focused file under the appropriate category and index it here.
- Do not place unrelated project, configuration, data-source, or general quantitative knowledge in `memory/rqalpha.md`; that file only guides compliant RQAlpha strategy work.
- Read only the memory relevant to the current task.
- Never store secrets or credentials in memory.
- Runtime state, raw tool output, todo state, and full session transcripts are not long-term memory.
